A split makes halves of any size,
so an Untyped smaller than the smallest region makes a frame no PMP entry describes.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: untyped outside granted memory, or not a block

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -233,7 +233,7 @@ static int op_untyped(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
     case OP_UNTYPED_SPLIT: {
         /* Each half is a block, so that a frame made of it is one NAPOT entry. */
         uint32_t half = size / 2;
-        if (!napot_block(base, half) || arg[1] == arg[2]) {
+        if (arg[1] == arg[2]) {
             return KERR_INVALID_ARG;
         }
         int err = cap_slot_free(table, arg[1]);
